@@ -39,3 +39,3 @@
 decision/aria-states-on-every-element · ARIA states written on every element — The accessibility builder writes the selected, toggled and invalid states from ARIA state attributes on every element, and an element whose role does not support an attribute reads it as one whose role does. · why: Ratified. · guard: accessibility_states · except: A select's option, whose selected state is its chosen state, with no aria-selected read.
-decision/changed-set-marks · What the engine's changed set marks — The engine's changed set marks a node's mutation, a focus or checked change, a text input, a select's changed choice, a single select's list opening or closing, a closing scroll included, and its highlight moving to another row; node creation, hover, active, other scrolls and layout do not. · why: Ratified, one item with the accessibility tree's refresh on change.
+decision/changed-set-marks · What the engine's changed set marks — The engine's changed set marks a node's mutation, a focus or checked change (post-layout focus loss too), a text input, a select's new choice, a single select's list opening or closing, by scroll too, and its highlight moving rows; node creation, hover, active, other scrolls and layout alone do not. · why: Ratified, one item with the accessibility tree's refresh on change.
 decision/harness-settle-leaves-changed-set · Harness settle leaves the changed set — A harness settle neither reads nor drains the changed set, and a freshly booted harness document holds a non-empty set, so a check that reads the set as what one step changed drains it first. · why: A settled step leaves the refresh and a later diff exactly what the step marked. · guard: stand_settle
@@ -111,5 +111,6 @@
 decision/falsy-boolean-attributes-removed · Falsy boolean attributes are removed — A falsy Dioxus value of one of the bridge's 28 boolean attributes removes the attribute on both the dynamic and the static template path, while a truthy value is still written. · why: Uses upstream's own boolean-attribute predicate, the mutation writer kept identical to upstream's. · guard: dioxus_falsy_boolean_attrs, dioxus_falsy_disabled · except: An attribute outside the list holding false, such as aria-hidden or a data- attribute, is still written as "false".
-decision/focus-fixup-reads-inert-alone · Focus fixup reads inertness alone — A focused node that becomes inert gives focus up at the flush, in every document, with no DOM blur or focusout; disabled and hidden take no part, so a focused control that no longer shows keeps focus and takes keys while the tree's focus names the window, a named SC 2.4.3 gap. · why: The limit of reading inertness alone was ratified. · guard: inert_subtree; key_press_after_container_lost_its_box
+decision/focus-fixup-gives-up-unshown-focus · Focus fixup gives up inert or unshown focus — A focused node gives focus up with no DOM blur or focusout, in every document: at the flush when it becomes inert, and after each layout when it no longer shows; a display: contents control and one beside a hidden sibling keep focus. · why: Ratified, with the Tab walk's skip of unshown nodes remedying the Tab trap the post-layout fixup alone made. · guard: inert_subtree; focus_fixup_unshown; key_press_after_container_lost_its_box
 decision/focus-stays-on-select-with-list-open · Focus stays on a select while its list is open — Focus stays on a select while its list is open, and the Tab walk holds with the list open and after each close. · why: pinned by the_tree_reads_the_list_open_on_the_select_its_focus_staying_there and escape_closes_with_the_value_unchanged_and_the_rows_back_at_the_selects_box
 decision/focus-visible-never-matches · :focus-visible never matches, :focus does — The :focus-visible selector never matches, while :focus and :focus-within do. · why: the stand task stylesheets (flight booker, temperature converter, cells) draw their focus cue with :focus rules, which match where :focus-visible would not
+decision/focus-within-hidden-holder-limit · Focus-within rule hiding its holder, a stated limit — A control whose own :focus-within rule hides its container still takes Tab and loses focus at the next layout. · guard: focus_fixup_unshown
 decision/focusability-recomputed-on-attribute-write · Focusability recomputed on tabindex, href, disabled — Cached focusability is recomputed when tabindex, href or disabled is set or removed, so a roving tabindex works. · why: pinned by a_tabindex_set_after_creation_takes_effect in the focusability_updates tests; roving-tabindex widgets rely on it
@@ -129,3 +130,3 @@
 decision/synthetic-click-at-node-centre · Synthetic click is a primary click at the centre — A synthetic click is a primary mouse click at the node's center. · why: Enter and Space activation, label click forwarding and the Dioxus event bridge build their synthetic Click from it
-decision/tab-and-shift-tab-move-focus · Tab and Shift+Tab move focus with focus events — Tab moves focus to the next focusable node and Shift+Tab to the previous one, dispatching focus events. · why: pinned by tab_and_shift_tab_walk_the_stated_sequence_and_wrap and tab_and_shift_tab_skip_an_inert_subtree; the driver's press tab relies on it
+decision/tab-and-shift-tab-move-focus · Tab and Shift+Tab move focus with focus events — Tab moves focus to the next focusable node and Shift+Tab to the previous one, dispatching focus events, in every document, skipping a node that does not show: out of the document, under display: none, or not visibility: visible. · why: pinned by tab_and_shift_tab_walk_the_stated_sequence_and_wrap and tab_and_shift_tab_skip_an_inert_subtree; the driver's press tab relies on it
 decision/tab-chooses-and-closes-select-list · Tab chooses the row and closes the list first — With a select's list open, Tab chooses the current row and closes the list before moving focus, in either direction. · why: pinned by tab_chooses_and_closes_before_focus_moves_either_way in the select_popup tests
